    "narrative": "The Austin Waves are primed for a high-ceiling outing today, headlined by **Gunnar Henderson** (83.29), who earns the top spot in our lineup against Arrighetti. While the park factors for **Gunnar Henderson** are slightly depressed, his elite 16% SP skill advantage and the 85% stolen base probability\u2014driven by a slow delivery from the mound\u2014make him our premier asset in our quest to dominate the scarcity of the SB category. **Jackson Merrill** (75.10) and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (74.56) follow closely behind; both benefit from massive SP skill boosts and optimal batting order slots, providing high-efficiency production that anchors our daily scoring floor. **Jacob Wilson** (74.08) also cracks the 70s as a high-upside play, leveraging a strong park factor and a favorable matchup against Littell.\n\nOur strategy today heavily exploits pitching vulnerabilities, specifically with **Cole Carrigg** (71.23) and **Sam Antonacci** (63.14). **Cole Carrigg** benefits from a massive 14% park boost, while **Sam Antonacci** capitalizes on a 19% SP skill advantage against the struggling Bieber. Conversely, the most difficult decision on our bench involved **Josh Jung** (43.31), who narrowly missed the cut. While **Josh Jung** remains a viable depth piece, the decision to bench him was purely mathematical; his 19% penalty against Murphy\u2019s pitch profile dropped him below the required efficiency threshold compared to the high-platoon alignment of **Miguel Vargas** (62.64), who retains his spot despite the tougher matchup due to an elite 0.401 xwOBA.\n\nManagers should monitor the status of **Drake Baldwin** (58.73), as he sits near our marginal floor. His strong position in the leadoff spot provides some security, but his matchup against Gore is the most volatile in our starting nine. We have intentionally benched **Liam Hicks** (36.73) and **Denzer Guzman** (35.13), as both players fell below our established 40.0 floor; despite the talent, keeping these bats on ice is essential for managing our remaining game caps in this 5x5 Roto push. We are banking on the speed and park-adjusted efficiency of our starters to bridge the gap in HR and SB categories without sacrificing our AVG standing.",
